-- coa29-sch8.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), 2006 c. 46, SCHEDULE 8 "Index of defined expressions".
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Generated by work/gen_sch8.py (the table is copied from the text by script) and work/build.py (quote lines from
-- srcrefs.py).
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk (Open Government Licence v3.0) made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Line numbers are of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
-- TARGET. The stable `l4` (main) 1.6.110.
--
-- WHAT THIS SCHEDULE IS. Section 1174 (the keel's) says Schedule 8 is an index of provisions that define or explain expressions used in the Act.
-- It states no rule of its own: each row says where an expression is defined. It is encoded as data (one record per row, in the Schedule's
-- order, in the Schedule's words) with one lookup. An expression the index does not list answers NOTHING (the index is silent; it does not
-- say the expression is undefined). The rows the text shows as dots are blank in this text and are not entries; a dots row inside a group
-- does not end it (the dash rows after the dots row at line 19685 are scopes of "company", like the three before it).
--
-- A row is: the expression as printed; the expression without its trailing scope (in Part 15), (for the purposes of Part 22); the scope (from
-- the parenthesis or from a row that begins with a dash under a head row); and the provision as printed.

§ `Schedule 8 -- Index of defined expressions`

DECLARE `sch 8 entry` HAS
    `sch 8 expression as printed` IS A STRING
    `sch 8 expression without its scope` IS A STRING
    `sch 8 scope` IS A STRING
    `sch 8 provision` IS A STRING

